@startuml
title Successful cancellation through the real Rails route
actor User
participant BookingsController
participant "Rails configuration" as Config
participant CancellationService
participant CancellationPolicy
participant Booking
User -> BookingsController: POST /:locale/bookings/:id/cancel
BookingsController -> BookingsController: authenticate, find scoped booking, authorize
BookingsController -> Config: configured policy factory
Config --> BookingsController: selected policy object
BookingsController -> CancellationService: new(booking, policy: policy).call
group Booking.with_lock transaction (repeated cancellation rejected)
CancellationService -> Booking: with_lock
Booking --> CancellationService: row lock acquired
CancellationService -> CancellationPolicy: cancellable?(booking, at: at)
CancellationPolicy --> CancellationService: true
CancellationService -> CancellationPolicy: refund_amount(booking, at: at)
CancellationPolicy --> CancellationService: refund
CancellationService -> Booking: update!(canceled_at: at,\n cancellation_refund_amount: refund)
Booking --> CancellationService: persisted booking
end
CancellationService --> BookingsController: booking + refund_amount result
BookingsController --> User: redirect to booking; refund notice
note over CancellationService, Booking
  Records the calculated refund amount.
  Does not send a Stripe refund request.
end note
@enduml
